    <div class="ans-block">
      <div class="ans-label">Full Exam Answer</div>
      <strong>Definition:</strong> A lithium-ion battery is a rechargeable secondary battery that uses lithium ions as primary charge carriers between cathode and anode during charge/discharge cycles.<br><br>
      <strong>Key Components:</strong>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Cathode (+):</strong> LiCoO₂ (Lithium Cobalt Oxide) — source of lithium ions. Determines voltage &amp; capacity.</li>
        <li><strong>Anode (-):</strong> Graphite (LiC₆) — stores Li ions during charging.</li>
        <li><strong>Electrolyte:</strong> Lithium salt in organic solvent — channel between cathode and anode.</li>
        <li><strong>Separator:</strong> Separates anode and cathode materials.</li>
      </ol>
      <strong>Reaction:</strong> CoO₂ + Li⁺ + e⁻ → LiCoO₂ (cathode reduction); LiC₆ → C₆ + Li⁺ + e⁻ (anode oxidation)<br><br>
      <strong>Advantages of Li-Ion Battery:</strong>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Low Maintenance:</strong> No periodic top-up or discharge required (unlike lead-acid batteries).</li>
        <li><strong>Available in Various Sizes:</strong> From smart watch to electric vehicles.</li>
        <li><strong>High Energy Density:</strong> Can provide power for long duration; compact size.</li>
        <li><strong>Low Self-Discharge Rate:</strong> Only ~1-2% per month after initial 4 hours.</li>
        <li><strong>High Voltage:</strong> 3.6V constant per cell (vs 1.5V for conventional).</li>
      </ol>
      <strong>Applications:</strong> Smartphones, laptops, EVs, pacemakers, portable power banks, solar energy storage, drones, aerospace.
    </div>
    <div class="kw-block"><div class="ans-label">Keywords</div>LiCoO₂, Graphite anode, 3.6V, low self-discharge, high energy density, electrolyte, separator, rechargeable, non-volatile ions</div>
    <div class="trick-block"><div class="ans-label">Memory Trick</div>Advantages: "L A H L H" → Low maintenance, Available in sizes, High energy density, Low self-discharge, High voltage</div>
  </div>

